Syed Mahmud Hossain, J. This Civil petition for Leave to Appeal is directed against the judgment and order dated the 7.10.2010 passed by the High Court Division in Civil Revision No. 1381 of 2007 discharging the Rule and affirming the judgment and decree dated 16.10.2010 passed by the learned Joint District judge, Additional Court, Comilla in Title Appeal No. 156 of 2004 allowing appeal and reversing the judgment and decree dated 13.05.2004 passed by the learned Assistant Judge, Brahmanpara, Comilla in Title Suit No. 35 of 2001 dismissing the suit. The facts, leading to the filing of this Civil Petition for Leave to Appeal in brief, are; 

 4. The trial court upon hearing the parties by its judgment and order dated 13.05.2014 dismissed the suit. Against that judgment and decree of the trial court, the defendant preferred Title Appeal No. 156 of 2004 before the learned District Judge, Comilla. On transfer, the appeal was heard and disposed of by the then learned Joint District Judge, Additional Court, Comilla, who by his judgment and order dated 16.10.2006 allowed the appeal reversing the judgment and decree of the trial court. 

 5. Being aggrieved by and dissatisfied with the judgment and decree passed by the appellate court, the plaintiffs preferred a revisional application before the High Court Division and obtained Rule in Civil Revision No. 1381 of 2007. The learned Single Judge of the High Court Division, by the judgment and order dated 07.10.2010 discharged the Rule without any order as to costs.
